    <string name="play_perf_profiles">Performance profiles</string>
    <string name="play_perf_ayn_only">AYN devices only</string>
    <string name="play_perf_ayn_only_help">On an AYN handheld, Tandem can set the performance mode, fan mode and refresh rate while a game plays, per game or for all of them. This device doesn\'t have AYN\'s modes, so there is nothing to set here.</string>
    <string name="play_perf_ayn_only_toast">This device doesn\'t have AYN\'s performance modes</string>
    <string name="play_perf_needs_shizuku">Needs Shizuku</string>
    <string name="play_perf_needs_shizuku_help">Set the performance mode, fan mode and refresh rate while a game plays, and put them back after. Tandem changes them the way AYN\'s control centre does; Android lets only the shell write those keys, so this needs Shizuku running with Tandem allowed.</string>
    <string name="play_perf_needs_shizuku_toast">This needs Shizuku running, with Tandem allowed</string>
    <string name="play_perf_mode">Performance mode</string>
    <string name="play_perf_mode_help">The AYN performance mode while a game plays: Standard, Performance or High performance. Keep leaves whatever is set. It goes back to how it was when you come back to Tandem; a game\'s own choice (Y on the game) wins over this.</string>
    <string name="play_perf_fan">Fan mode</string>
    <string name="play_perf_fan_help">The fan while a game plays: Off, Quiet, Smart or Sport. Keep leaves whatever is set, and a custom speed from AYN\'s app is always left alone.</string>
    <string name="play_perf_refresh">Refresh rate</string>
    <string name="play_perf_refresh_help">The top screen\'s refresh rate while a game plays. 60 Hz saves battery and heat; 120 Hz is smoother for games that can run that fast. Keep leaves whatever is set.</string>
